00:02:00.010 --> 00:02:06.520
Welcome back, Rinna , Shipon , Kouta 

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:05.350
Episode Eighteen: 
Distant Voice

00:02:01.850 --> 00:02:03.650
Welcome back! 

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:21.220
I'm so moved.

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:24.330
I can't believe you really sang and danced for us.

00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:27.810
We never thought we would be the ones watching it, after all.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:28.710
Yeah.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:34.530
Originally, this was Shipon's idea for Rinna...

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:36.520
...who was coming from the Ultima.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:38.120
It was really great.

00:02:38.690 --> 00:02:40.710
Especially Akira as the prince!

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:41.150
What?

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:46.420
Now, let us dance, princess.

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:54.280
Er... no... that is...

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:56.970
Wasn't it hard to practice?

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:58.700
Good of you to ask.

00:02:59.020 --> 00:03:02.230
I worked so hard, I failed Introductory Aviation.

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:03.470
Really?

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:09.600
There's no relation between our practicing and your failing!

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:11.080
It was so easy, too.

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:13.770
But in exchange, I passed Telecommunications Training, right?

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:14.980
Yeah...?

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:15.960
That's unusual...

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:17.260
Unusual?!

00:03:17.580 --> 00:03:18.680
Er... no...

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:23.110
I set the speed record for Extravehicular Maintenance.

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:26.490
I got licenses for two kinds of heavy equipment.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.030
And I also mastered the cakes at Early's.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:32.160
Wow, everyone's incredible.

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:34.990
Well, over 80 days have passed, after all.

00:03:41.210 --> 00:03:44.850
That's true... 80 days have passed, haven't they...

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:48.580
That being true, how were your 80 days?

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:49.850
Oh... Right.

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:52.590
What happened with the Ultima is classified...

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:55.460
...so we can't really talk about it, but...

00:03:55.870 --> 00:03:59.220
Oh, but it looks like we've made up with Miss Machida.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:01.130
That, and Miss Leila...

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:01.930
No, no...

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:03.680
I'm talking about Kouta.

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:04.300
Huh?

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:09.310
You spent 80 days with him without nuisances like us, right?

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:10.270
What?!

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:11.400
How did it go?

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:15.300
Don't tell me you went so far you can't tell us.

00:04:15.300 --> 00:04:16.570
N-No...

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:19.000
Oh, I see...

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.250
Right, right.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:20.970
Shut up...

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:24.030
It's no different than how we were before we left. .

00:04:21.750 --> 00:04:23.370
...I didn't do it because I wanted to...

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:25.480
What? You were so up for it. At all?

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:25.650
At all?

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:26.200
Uh-uh...

00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:29.820
What is it?

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:33.140
Huh?

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:40.170
Using an unknown method, the unidentified flying objects...

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:43.520
...moved the Ultima into the Cosmic Fracture.

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:47.250
The unidentified flying objects ability to appear at will...

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:49.860
...is probably achieved through the same method.

00:04:52.020 --> 00:04:55.890
They put the Ultima's gravity control systems into overload...

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:59.950
...and made it produce a degenerating micro black hole.

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:09.760
Of course, a black hole of that size is unstable...

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:12.900
...so it immediately evaporated.

00:05:13.310 --> 00:05:16.290
As it disappeared, it gave off X-ray bursts.

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:19.670
The dimensional vibrations caused by this...

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:21.690
...interfered with the Cosmic Fracture...

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:25.710
...and reduced its advance speed to 1/35 of what it was.

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:28.110
Because of this, the Fracture will arrive...

00:05:28.190 --> 00:05:30.830
...in the Sol System in 100 days, starting three days ago.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:34.450
So, according to current time, approximately 60 days from now.

00:05:34.730 --> 00:05:37.310
What will happen when the Fracture arrives?

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:39.390
Will we be swallowed up by the tear?

00:05:39.970 --> 00:05:42.800
We are currently investigating the effects the Fracture...

00:05:42.980 --> 00:05:46.730
...will have on the Sol System, but we lack any real data.

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:49.080
So after the wave is the himo?

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:52.890
Are you saying the unidentified flying objects saved us?

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:55.610
The fact that the advance has been slowed is definite.

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:59.210
We've just finished the Great Mission, yet...

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.840
Well, in any case...

00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:04.720
...we need information.

00:06:05.360 --> 00:06:06.750
Correct information.

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:28.000
No way. Rinna, you're not staying with Shipon in her room?

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:31.320
No, this time I'm with my dad and my mom.

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:33.900
We got a house in the S5 district.

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:37.140
Next time, would it be okay for us to come and hang out at your place?

00:06:37.450 --> 00:06:38.260
Please come!

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:41.860
The cake my mom makes is really delicious!

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:44.050
It might be better for you to refuse them.

00:06:44.390 --> 00:06:46.820
They might eat your portion, too, after all.

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:47.920
What?

00:06:47.980 --> 00:06:50.290
Arisa, the next class is in the B3 classroom.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:53.330
Oh. I didn't tell you, Shipon?

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:56.630
I changed over to the maintenance course...

00:06:57.030 --> 00:06:59.260
...so our specialty classes are different.

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:00.880
O-Oh, I see...

00:07:01.110 --> 00:07:04.430
When I tried it, doing maintenance was more fun than being a pilot, so...

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:07.410
You are really good at maintenance, Arisa.

00:07:07.930 --> 00:07:08.860
Aren't I, though?

00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:12.070
Arisa! If you don't hurry, you'll be late!

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:13.860
Today we're practicing engine maintenance!

00:07:14.010 --> 00:07:14.620
Oh!

00:07:15.020 --> 00:07:16.030
I forgot!

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:18.110
Wait!

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:19.130
Did you do the homework?

00:07:19.440 --> 00:07:20.130
Of course.

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:22.020
What? Teach me later.

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:24.470
Seriously.

00:07:25.370 --> 00:07:26.790
That was a meaningless meeting.

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:31.370
All they did was confirm that they don't know anything.

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:34.180
That's important.

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:37.020
Knowing that you don't know something...

00:07:37.570 --> 00:07:40.230
Is that the "knowledge of ignorance?"

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:43.020
Yes, yes, that's it.

00:07:44.340 --> 00:07:46.710
I didn't offer this at the meeting...

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:51.540
...but I have my own thoughts about the unidentified flying objects.

00:07:55.990 --> 00:07:57.000
Let me hear them.

00:07:57.610 --> 00:08:00.840
I think they might be aliens.

00:08:04.960 --> 00:08:05.820
It's a check.

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:10.800
Do you think aliens would be like the ones in the comics?

00:08:11.430 --> 00:08:11.940
No...

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:14.040
It's an interesting deduction.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:16.550
Their technology is different as well...

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:21.870
...and their design lines appear to be different from those of earthlings.

00:08:22.480 --> 00:08:23.350
I see.

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:27.860
And those strange sounds that were heard during the Ultima's explosion...

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:31.070
I've come to realize there's a chance they were words.

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:34.050
There is also a chance that it's a disguise.

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:35.530
Certainly.

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:40.100
But wouldn't it be arrogant to think that the only intelligent beings...

00:08:40.180 --> 00:08:42.690
...in this universe are we earthlings?

00:08:47.350 --> 00:08:48.550
It's a checkmate.

00:08:55.360 --> 00:08:57.440
Akira! Over here!

00:08:57.610 --> 00:08:58.800
Over...
Stop.

00:08:59.870 --> 00:09:00.330
What?

00:09:00.590 --> 00:09:01.050
Look.

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:07.010
The two of them are going out.

00:09:07.190 --> 00:09:08.110
What?!

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:09.320
Really? Really?

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:11.150
You're too loud, Shipon.

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:12.390
But, but...

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:15.460
It looks like she was fond of him from the beginning.

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:16.790
I see...

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:21.380
80 days have passed, after all. A lot of things have happened...

00:09:21.670 --> 00:09:22.660
Exactly.

00:09:23.470 --> 00:09:24.250
Miss Fujisawa.

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:28.410
They say there are too few cakes for the ceremony.

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:29.510
By how many?

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:31.600
Um... They say 150.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:32.860
That many?

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:38.440
I've been given responsibility for the regular students' graduation party.

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:39.690
Amazing!

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:44.170
It's customary for the students to run the Stellvia's school events, after all.

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:47.760
Like when the regular students had that welcoming party for us.

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:49.920
This time it's our turn.

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:52.010
Yayoi, does that mean...

00:09:52.090 --> 00:09:53.890
...you're the Big Four of the preparatory students?

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:56.360
It's nothing that grandiose.

00:09:56.750 --> 00:09:59.700
Hey, didn't we make an extra 10%?

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:02.530
It looks like we didn't factor in the families.

00:10:02.940 --> 00:10:06.230
Try and see if we can't place an additional order with the bakery.

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:08.750
And how are the fireworks coming along?

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:11.150
Right. When I asked my big sister, she said it was okay.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:12.940
Thank you, that's a big help.

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:14.610
Tony was looking for you.

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:17.110
He said he wanted to discuss the time schedule.

00:10:19.710 --> 00:10:22.440
I see... 80 days have passed.

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:25.660
I'd better do my best, too!

00:10:26.070 --> 00:10:28.070
We have only 60 days in our time limit.

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:30.590
We know too little about the unidentified flying objects...

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:34.220
...and the same goes for the Cosmic Fracture.

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:37.430
Because of that, we could only calm the council by saying...

00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:40.640
...we'd have another conference after gathering more information.

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:43.280
And you want to use Infi to gather the information?

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:45.070
Can we count on you?

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:47.550
Yes, but by myself, I can't...

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:50.790
We're getting someone ready to be your support operator.

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:54.640
We plan on getting an excellent person from headquarters.

00:10:55.100 --> 00:10:58.250
Even still, getting used to the DLS will take some time...

00:10:58.690 --> 00:10:59.840
About that...

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:04.560
I would really like to recommend Shima Katase for the support role.

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:07.300
But... she's still a preparatory student.

00:11:07.570 --> 00:11:08.630
So am I.

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:11.500
It'll be all right if it's Shima-chan doing it.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:33.160
Please put in number three and number six!

00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:35.010
Please take care of modifying the alpha later.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:37.880
The backup module goes in from the left! The left!

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:43.990
I wonder... if it'll be all right with me doing this.

00:11:44.350 --> 00:11:45.620
It'll work if you're doing it, Shima-chan.

00:11:48.570 --> 00:11:50.250
How is it, you two?

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:51.500
It's satisfactory!

00:11:51.980 --> 00:11:53.870
I still can't say.

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:56.340
It's basically the same as before.

00:11:56.840 --> 00:11:57.880
Try and take a look.

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:09.070
We've made the system more sensitive for observation.

00:12:09.850 --> 00:12:13.670
So you might see too much information.

00:12:14.070 --> 00:12:14.950
It'll be all right.

00:12:15.490 --> 00:12:17.800
If that happens, I'll close one eye.

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:21.300
Try not to close both eyes.

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:24.710
Shima-chan, we can start at Level F, right?

00:12:25.030 --> 00:12:27.060
What? Y-Yeah.

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:29.690
Please begin.

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:33.620
From Level F, skipping the initialization sequence.

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:40.990
Yeah. Nothing's really changed. In that case, this will work.

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:41.630
What?

00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:43.220
Let's try some minor movements.

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:46.550
We're going to start from the high part of Type-12, Shima-chan.

00:12:47.010 --> 00:12:47.890
R-Right.

00:12:50.860 --> 00:12:52.270
I'm going to have some free time.

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:55.630
The Katies have been collected, and their engines are being exchanged.

00:12:55.940 --> 00:12:56.690
I see.

00:12:57.390 --> 00:12:58.470
Exchanged...

00:12:58.750 --> 00:13:00.270
Are they going to increase their output?

00:13:00.570 --> 00:13:03.440
Probably... So they can move alongside Infi.

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:05.490
As escorts?

00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:06.760
Probably.

00:13:07.190 --> 00:13:07.780
I see...

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:11.080
Ayaka... 
Mm?

00:13:11.790 --> 00:13:13.120
Take care of Shipon...

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:15.640
...please.

00:13:16.450 --> 00:13:19.250
Her skills are beyond those of a student.

00:13:19.800 --> 00:13:20.700
Even mine...

00:13:21.020 --> 00:13:22.230
That's not it. 
 What?

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:29.570
There may have been times when she's been discouraged...

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:32.810
...but I think Shipon is going to hit it soon...

00:13:34.090 --> 00:13:36.310
The unseen wall of the self.

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:40.450
It was your first time. That's why it was like that.

00:13:41.030 --> 00:13:42.530
Once you get used to it, it won't be anything.

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:43.740
Right...

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:45.330
More importantly...

00:13:45.390 --> 00:13:49.700
...Masaru said they're going to Rinna's place on the 17th.

00:13:50.280 --> 00:13:51.350
You're okay with that, right?

00:13:51.550 --> 00:13:51.990
Yeah.

00:13:52.800 --> 00:13:56.290
But before that, we have to end this mission...

00:13:57.220 --> 00:13:59.240
Otoyama, can I see you a second?
Sure.

00:14:00.050 --> 00:14:00.660
See you later.

00:14:01.270 --> 00:14:02.250
Take it easy and get some rest.

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:03.060
Okay.

00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:10.810
I can't do this like Kouta can...

00:14:13.330 --> 00:14:17.350
No, no. If I get depressed, I'll go back to being how I was.

00:14:19.570 --> 00:14:22.350
If you can't do something, then all you have to do is practice! Yeah!

00:14:25.410 --> 00:14:26.790
Oh, Akira!

00:14:27.350 --> 00:14:28.880
You're going to use the simulators too, Akira?

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:30.360
How about we do it together?

00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:33.790
Is that okay?

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:37.240
Oh, maybe you're going to meet up with Jojo? In that case...

00:14:37.300 --> 00:14:37.990
That's not it...

00:14:38.220 --> 00:14:38.600
What?

00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:41.720
I'm not like you or Kouta...

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:44.270
I can't do it as skillfully as you can.

00:14:44.560 --> 00:14:45.570
I'm not a genius.

00:14:46.090 --> 00:14:48.630
That's not... I'm not a genius...

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:53.460
You won in astroball, and you were chosen as a pilot for Infi.

00:14:54.190 --> 00:14:58.410
You just lightly jump over walls that I work hard to overcome...

00:14:59.590 --> 00:15:02.400
We've finally come to the point where I can't even compare the two of us...

00:15:03.260 --> 00:15:03.890
That's why...

00:15:29.490 --> 00:15:30.820
I'm not a genius...

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:35.300
I'm not a genius, either...

00:15:53.460 --> 00:15:55.050
Hi, this is Rinna!

00:15:56.380 --> 00:16:00.950
Oh, Rinna. I don't have a reason for calling, but can we talk for a bit?

00:16:01.190 --> 00:16:02.690
Rinna, who's calling?

00:16:02.800 --> 00:16:05.250
It's Shipon. You know her, right, Dad?

00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:07.350
The cake is going to finish baking soon.

00:16:07.690 --> 00:16:10.530
Then maybe I'll eat your piece, Rinna.

00:16:10.530 --> 00:16:11.290
What?!

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:12.990
Dad, you're mean!

00:16:13.210 --> 00:16:14.430
I hope you get fat!

00:16:14.920 --> 00:16:17.700
Oh, but aren't your friends coming to visit on the 17th?

00:16:17.930 --> 00:16:18.610
Oh...

00:16:18.880 --> 00:16:20.790
I don't want an uncool Dad!

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:22.670
I don't like that at all!

00:16:22.760 --> 00:16:25.680
Rinna, I'm sorry, I'll call back later. 

00:16:23.510 --> 00:16:24.900
Are you listening, Dad?

00:16:29.520 --> 00:16:30.480
Tada!

00:16:31.490 --> 00:16:33.520
Wow, incredible!

00:16:33.860 --> 00:16:34.450
What do you think?

00:16:34.610 --> 00:16:37.070
It's a sample of the graduation party cakes that Milady prepared.

00:16:37.190 --> 00:16:38.200
I got one for us.

00:16:38.370 --> 00:16:39.300
I see.

00:16:39.730 --> 00:16:43.430
This is to celebrate you being officially chosen as one of Infi's pilots.

00:16:44.620 --> 00:16:48.200
Congratulations. As your best friend, I'm proud of you.

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:51.270
Who did you hear that from? That's horrible.

00:16:51.640 --> 00:16:54.390
And I was thinking I'd keep quiet and surprise you...

00:16:56.100 --> 00:16:59.280
I can't believe that you've become such an incredible person, Shipon.

00:16:59.630 --> 00:17:00.840
That's quite the accomplishment!

00:17:04.250 --> 00:17:05.250
Hmm...

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:10.090
Although, you don't look so much like an incredible person.

00:17:11.540 --> 00:17:13.820
Actually, I don't really feel like one, either.

00:17:16.540 --> 00:17:16.890
Here.

00:17:22.820 --> 00:17:23.600
Arisa...
Shipon.

00:17:24.730 --> 00:17:26.690
If you ever have a problem, tell me.

00:17:26.980 --> 00:17:27.330
What?

00:17:27.880 --> 00:17:30.070
Well, piloting Infi is impossible, but I'll do what I can to help.

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:34.010
I'll do your homework, answer for you during roll call.

00:17:34.090 --> 00:17:35.080
You can ask me anything.

00:17:35.190 --> 00:17:36.310
Uh... Right...

00:17:36.810 --> 00:17:38.780
You have an incredible talent, Shipon.

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:41.010
As your best friend, I guarantee that.

00:17:41.410 --> 00:17:42.620
So let me help you.

00:17:43.260 --> 00:17:46.150
I want you to become a wonderful pilot, after all.

00:17:58.040 --> 00:18:00.120
The cleanup of A-block's airspace has been confirmed.

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:01.070
All green.

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:01.830
Roger.

00:18:02.690 --> 00:18:05.300
We have passed three hours until the mission begins.

00:18:05.380 --> 00:18:08.040
All department leaders, please report your situation.

00:18:08.820 --> 00:18:11.170
Leave everything from Phase 54 to Otoyama.

00:18:11.710 --> 00:18:14.430
You've heard that the procedure for 115 has ended up backwards.

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:15.450
Yes, ma'am.

00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:17.530
What's wrong? Are you nervous?

00:18:18.050 --> 00:18:19.550
A little.
I see.

00:18:20.390 --> 00:18:22.150
It's better to be a little nervous.

00:18:22.850 --> 00:18:24.320
Having a moderate amount of stress...

00:18:24.350 --> 00:18:26.200
Um, Miss Leila?

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:32.370
This is important work related to the future of all of humanity, right?

00:18:32.970 --> 00:18:35.020
Is it okay for me to be on that kind of mission?

00:18:35.430 --> 00:18:37.220
Yeah, I was surprised too.

00:18:38.000 --> 00:18:39.970
That "that Katase" came this far.

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:43.030
A new age, system...

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:45.780
A new era is coming.

00:18:45.920 --> 00:18:46.330
What?

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:48.120
Thank you, Katase.

00:18:48.700 --> 00:18:50.580
I didn't start this job because I wanted to...

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:54.570
...but from my heart, I feel glad that I became a teacher.

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:55.580
Uh...

00:19:01.600 --> 00:19:02.410
We're counting on you.

00:19:02.610 --> 00:19:03.040
Yes, ma'am.

00:19:04.980 --> 00:19:06.340
I'm sorry I'm late.

00:19:06.630 --> 00:19:08.160
I'll start on Phase 11 immediately.

00:19:08.650 --> 00:19:09.690
Kouta!

00:19:10.180 --> 00:19:13.050
Kouta, I have no confidence.

00:19:13.420 --> 00:19:14.580
I don't either.

00:19:14.980 --> 00:19:16.750
Because the future of mankind could be decided...

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:18.630
...by the information that we gather.

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:20.680
It's too heavy a responsibility.

00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:22.590
That's not what I mean...

00:19:22.710 --> 00:19:25.940
It's all right. Taking responsibility is the work of the people above us.

00:19:26.460 --> 00:19:28.460
All we have to do is complete the mission we've been given.

00:19:29.360 --> 00:19:30.250
Phase 10 has been cleared.

00:19:31.000 --> 00:19:32.360
Will it be possible to do Phase 11?

00:19:32.830 --> 00:19:34.850
Go ahead. Entering Phase 11.

00:19:35.170 --> 00:19:38.640
Roger. Beginning phase. Monitor number one, on.

00:19:39.390 --> 00:19:40.750
Monitor number one, on.

00:19:41.670 --> 00:19:43.350
Please start the DLS.

00:19:43.990 --> 00:19:45.290
Starting the system.

00:19:50.470 --> 00:19:53.820
Run, Masaru! It's your fault we're late!

00:19:53.850 --> 00:19:55.760
You can go on ahead!

00:19:55.760 --> 00:19:57.720
No we can't! We're all going to see them off!

00:20:01.920 --> 00:20:02.990
120 seconds to go...

00:20:04.170 --> 00:20:04.780
115...

00:20:06.340 --> 00:20:07.060
75...

00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:08.910
70...

00:20:10.160 --> 00:20:10.790
50...

00:20:11.890 --> 00:20:12.440
45...

00:20:13.020 --> 00:20:14.060
We made it!

00:20:13.600 --> 00:20:14.010
40...

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:14.960
Fire! 

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:23.370
Five...

00:20:24.150 --> 00:20:24.530
Four...

00:20:25.510 --> 00:20:25.860
Three...

00:20:26.670 --> 00:20:27.100
Two...

00:20:27.910 --> 00:20:28.380
One...

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:29.440
Zero!

00:20:30.340 --> 00:20:31.470
The launch is successful.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:34.770
The Infinity is beginning its acceleration.

00:20:35.630 --> 00:20:38.500
It will be arriving in the observation area in 180 minutes.

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:48.670
Open the DLS.

00:20:49.020 --> 00:20:51.080
Roger. Opening the system.

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:56.610
I can see it...

00:20:57.060 --> 00:20:58.250
I can see the brilliance...

00:20:58.450 --> 00:20:59.520
Brilliance?

00:21:00.300 --> 00:21:01.880
You can see it, right, Shima-chan?

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:03.570
What?

00:21:04.170 --> 00:21:06.020
What... is this?

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:12.990
It might have been this brilliance...

00:21:13.830 --> 00:21:15.650
...that I've been searching for all this time.

00:21:17.480 --> 00:21:19.880
I'm not like you and Kouta.

00:21:20.160 --> 00:21:23.260
I want you to become a wonderful pilot, after all.

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:28.170
Shima-chan?

00:21:29.010 --> 00:21:30.080
I can't...

00:21:31.010 --> 00:21:31.590
...see it.

00:21:33.210 --> 00:21:34.450
I don't understand.

00:21:35.030 --> 00:21:36.180
I don't understand...

00:21:37.140 --> 00:21:40.810
I'm by myself. There's no one around me...

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
kono sora no iku hate ni

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
Where the end of this sky goes

00:21:55.960 --> 00:22:01.050
この空の行く果てに

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
mada mienu mirai no nami ga ri

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
Are waves of the future that cannot yet be seen

00:22:04.520 --> 00:22:10.970
まだ見えぬ 未来の波があり

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
ikite iru ikutsu mono unmei o koete yuku

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
We are alive; we overcome many destinies

00:22:12.190 --> 00:22:21.010
生きている いくつもの運命を越えて行く

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
dare ni osowari dare ni koute iru no darou

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
Who are we learning from, who are we asking?

00:22:21.440 --> 00:22:28.780
誰に教わり 誰に請うているのだろう

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
hito wa tsukiru inochi no aima ni

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
People do not have time to fear encountering

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:37.600
人は尽きる命の合間に

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
deau koto ni obieru ma wa nai

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
The space between expiring lives

00:22:37.890 --> 00:22:46.570
出会うことに 怯える間はない

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
tatoe kyou de kono sekai ga owarou to shite ite mo

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
Even if this world would end today

00:22:46.570 --> 00:22:57.240
たとえ今日で この世界が終わろうとしていても

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
kimi o ai suru darou

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
I will still love you

00:22:57.410 --> 00:23:02.820
君を愛するだろう

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:07.030
Next Episode

00:23:05.910 --> 00:23:06.780
This is Arisa!

00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:07.540
This is Rinna! 

00:23:07.820 --> 00:23:09.960
So about now, Shipon is all alone with Kouta.

00:23:10.190 --> 00:23:11.550
Argh! I'm so jealous!

00:23:11.610 --> 00:23:13.980
Huh? Do you like Kouta, Arisa?

00:23:15.220 --> 00:23:18.750
They're both so young, I feel jealous of both of them.

00:23:18.780 --> 00:23:23.440
Oh, but Shipon's so lucky to have someone like you to cheer her on.

00:23:23.490 --> 00:23:25.000
Then for now, I'll cheer for you.

00:23:25.170 --> 00:23:27.370
Hooray, hooray, Ri-n-na!

00:23:27.370 --> 00:23:29.540
All right! All right! All right!...

00:23:29.910 --> 00:23:33.080
On the next episode of Stellvia of the Universe, "Cry Baby, Hot-head"

00:23:32.050 --> 00:23:35.050
Episode Nineteen:
 Cry Baby, Hot-head

00:23:33.580 --> 00:23:34.910
Please watch!
